From 42671f6045aa06afd6ca1521aa643608e8462705 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Copeland <ben.copeland@linaro.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:31:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] clk: rockchip: pll: don't recurse when restoring the old
 rate fails

When a Rockchip PLL does not lock after being reprogrammed, its
set_params callback restores the previous settings by calling itself.
If the restore does not lock either, it calls itself again, without
bound, until the kernel stack overflows.

This was hit on an RK3399 board when a VPLL setting failed to lock
while being applied from assigned-clock-rates during probe:

  rockchip_rk3399_pll_set_params+0x1c4/0x1d0
  rockchip_rk3399_pll_set_rate+0x64/0x110
  clk_change_rate+0xdc/0x518
  clk_core_set_rate_nolock+0x2e0/0x3a8
  clk_set_rate+0x40/0x140
  of_clk_set_defaults+0x3c8/0x720
  platform_probe+0x40/0xc0
  ...
  Kernel panic - not syncing: kernel stack overflow

The restore path passes the settings read back from the hardware with
the rate field cleared, so use that to try the restore only once and
return the error if it fails too. Apply the same to the RK3036,
RK3066, RK3399 and RK3588 PLL types, which share the pattern.

Signed-off-by: Ben Copeland <ben.copeland@linaro.org>
---
 drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-pll.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-pll.c b/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-pll.c
index 706ca4b344d3..35a93a4886e3 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-pll.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-pll.c
@@ -241,7 +241,7 @@ static int rockchip_rk3036_pll_set_params(struct rockchip_clk_pll *pll,
 
 	/* wait for the pll to lock */
 	ret = rockchip_rk3036_pll_wait_lock(pll);
-	if (ret) {
+	if (ret && rate->rate) {
 		pr_warn("%s: pll update unsuccessful, trying to restore old params\n",
 			__func__);
 		rockchip_rk3036_pll_set_params(pll, &cur);
@@ -476,7 +476,7 @@ static int rockchip_rk3066_pll_set_params(struct rockchip_clk_pll *pll,
 
 	/* wait for the pll to lock */
 	ret = rockchip_pll_wait_lock(pll);
-	if (ret) {
+	if (ret && rate->rate) {
 		pr_warn("%s: pll update unsuccessful, trying to restore old params\n",
 			__func__);
 		rockchip_rk3066_pll_set_params(pll, &cur);
@@ -725,7 +725,7 @@ static int rockchip_rk3399_pll_set_params(struct rockchip_clk_pll *pll,
 
 	/* wait for the pll to lock */
 	ret = rockchip_rk3399_pll_wait_lock(pll);
-	if (ret) {
+	if (ret && rate->rate) {
 		pr_warn("%s: pll update unsuccessful, trying to restore old params\n",
 			__func__);
 		rockchip_rk3399_pll_set_params(pll, &cur);
@@ -981,7 +981,7 @@ static int rockchip_rk3588_pll_set_params(struct rockchip_clk_pll *pll,
 
 	/* wait for the pll to lock */
 	ret = rockchip_rk3588_pll_wait_lock(pll);
-	if (ret) {
+	if (ret && rate->rate) {
 		pr_warn("%s: pll update unsuccessful, trying to restore old params\n",
 			__func__);
 		rockchip_rk3588_pll_set_params(pll, &cur);
-- 
